Answer: 258
There was one problem for which I could not determine author information, so I set the author as one of the problem czars at random. Then, I ran the following command on a folder containing TeX solutions files to all four contests:

```
evan@ArchMega ~/Downloads/November
$ grep --no-filename "Proposed by: " *.tex | sort | uniq -c
    15 {\em Proposed by: Allen Liu }
    1 {\em Proposed by: Brice Huang }
    2 {\em Proposed by: Christopher Shao }
    2 {\em Proposed by: Daniel Qu }
    21 {\em Proposed by: Eshaan Nichani }
```

```
3 {\em Proposed by: Evan Chen }
{\em Proposed by: Henrik Boecken }
{\em Proposed by: Kevin Sun }
{\em Proposed by: Kevin Yang }
{\em Proposed by: Meghal Gupta }
{\em Proposed by: Rachel Zhang }
{\em Proposed by: Sam Korsky }
{\em Proposed by: Saranesh Prembabu }
{\em Proposed by: Shyam Narayanan }
```

This gave the counts of problem proposals; there were 14 distinct authors of problems for November 2016. Summing their ages (concealed for privacy) gives 258 .
